s it minimizes the risk of aiding opponents in forming melds and aligns with the goal of preserving terminal and honor tiles for potential high-scoring patterns like All Terminals and Honors.  \nReason: B6 is a middle tile with limited strategic value in the current hand. The player across already has B6 in their melds, reducing its utility for them. Discarding it allows retaining W8, W9 (terminals) and J3 (honor tile), which are critical for scoring patterns. Other options like W8 or W9 risk exposing high-value terminals, while T7 and J3 are less immediately exploitable.  \nAnswer: Play B6"}
